# Citation metadata (CFF 1.2.0) — renders GitHub's "Cite this repository"
# button (APA + BibTeX). Keep release-accurate: every release cut bumps
# `version` + `date-released`.
#
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "DICOM RT DVH Validation: an intermediate data layer for dose-volume parameter extraction"
abstract: >-
  Validation software for the use of DICOM RT DVH files at 1 cGy resolution as
  an intermediate caching layer between DICOM-RT source data held in a PACS and
  downstream clinical data repositories. From RT Dose and RT Structure Set
  inputs it writes one DICOM RT DVH object per structure (PS3.3 Section
  C.8.8.4), encoding the full differential dose-volume histogram, so that any
  dose-volume parameter (Vx, Dx, Dxcc, mean dose, gEUD, NTCP/TCP) can be derived
  later without returning to the PACS. Contains the computation and caching
  modules, the parameter extraction code, the six-phase experiment runner and
  the unit test suite used to validate the cache against analytical phantoms
  with closed-form DVHs, published reference values, and clinical plans from
  independent treatment planning systems.
